SUSPECTED BUG: the wrap of a nil error has no entry (same as loop_retry_single / is_errorf_wraps_nil).
Retry loop: nil -> return; Is(ErrTimeout) || Is(ErrRateLimited) -> continue; else fail fast with "job %s: %w";
after the loop "retries exhausted: %w" wraps the last error. With Max == 0 the loop never runs and the function
returns fmt.Errorf("...: %w", nil), a non-nil error wrapping nothing: expected an opaque fmt.Errorf entry
for it, actual: none.
Otherwise: ErrTimeout / ErrRateLimited only under "retries exhausted", ErrNotFound / *NetError under
"job %s: %w" - and, as a documented over-approximation, ALSO under "retries exhausted" (6 entries, run-time
truth 4 + the wrap of nil): the continue sits on the true side of an ||, which dominance-based guards do not
narrow (see is_or_true_branch).
-- args --
runner/runner.go:@run
